.SS "void VERUM_AUX_MEMORY_16B_copy (void *restrict destination, const void *restrict source)"

.PP
Copy exactly 128 bits (16 bytes) from \fRsource\fP to \fRdestination\fP\&. Fixed-width specialisation for 128-bit block transfers\&. Both pointers must be 4-byte aligned and must not overlap\&. Emits exactly four word-width loads and four word-width stores with no branching or runtime alignment probing\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIdestination\fP Target buffer\&. Must be 4-byte aligned\&. 
.br
\fIsource\fP Source buffer\&. Must be 4-byte aligned\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBPrecondition\fP
.RS 4
\fRdestination\fP and \fRsource\fP are non-NULL\&. 

.PP
Both pointers are aligned to \fRsizeof(uint32_t)\fP\&. 

.PP
The regions [\fRdestination\fP, \fRdestination\fP + 16) and [\fRsource\fP, \fRsource\fP + 16) do not overlap\&. 
.RE
.PP

